IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- New York Social Services Law, Article 5 -- family assistance (New York's TANF cash assistance) for a family household:
-- who it is given to (s 349 A, B, D; s 131(6)); the 60-month limit (s 350(2)); voluntarily quitting a job (s 131(10)); the
-- resources exempted (s 131-n(1)); the standard of need, the grant schedule, the home energy grants and the rounding and
-- $10 rules (s 131-a(1)-(3-d)); the earned income and child support disregards (s 131-a(8)); the shelter allowance paid to
-- the landlord (s 131-a(7)); and the fair hearing for a minor parent (s 131(6)).
--
-- SEAT: the applicant -- a parent, another relative caring for a child, or a pregnant individual -- applying for family
-- assistance. "Can my family get family assistance? How much a month? What counts against it? What happens if I quit my
-- job? Is there a time limit?" Provisions addressed to the social services official are encoded as what they mean for that
-- person: what the official may decide (asked as facts), what the district must pay and when it must not.
--
-- Edition: NYSenate.gov Open Legislation, each section's most recent revision as at 24 October 2026 (s 131: 2026-05-22;
-- s 131-a: 2025-11-07; s 131-n: 2025-08-01; s 349: 2014-09-22; s 350: 2022-07-01), deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/ny-ssl-art5-selected.txt.
--
-- Amounts set by regulation of the department (the shelter allowance, fuel for heating), the June adjustment of the 50
-- percent earned income disregard (s 131-a(8)(a)(ii)) and the federal poverty level are not in the deposited text; they are
-- inputs. Read with the federal Social Security Act encoding (Title IV-A, subjects/us/social-security-act/) for the
-- federal TANF frame; cross-folder IMPORT is not possible in the stable l4.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: safety net assistance (ss 157-165), to which a family that reaches the 60-month limit is in practice moved;
-- emergency assistance; the stepparent deeming of s 131-a(9) and the lump sum rule of s 131-a(12) (inputs only through
-- "other countable income"); the HIV rent cap of s 131-a(14), (15); the special items of s 131-a(5); the work rules of
-- s 131(7) and Article 5 Title 9-B beyond s 131(5) as an input; the disregards of s 131-a(8)(a)(vii), (ix)-(xii).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the applicant's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `New York Social Services Law Article 5 -- family assistance`

§§ `s 349 -- who family assistance is given to`

-- s 349 A: "Family assistance shall be given to a pregnant individual, a parent or other relative as herein specified for
-- the benefit of a child under eighteen years of age, or of a child under nineteen years of age who is a full-time student
-- regularly attending a secondary school or in the equivalent level of vocational or technical training if, in the judgment
-- of the social services official: 1. the granting of an allowance will be in the interest of such child, and 2. the parent
-- or other relative is a fit person to bring up such child ..., and 3. such child is a resident of the state on the date of
-- application for aid." B.1: the child must be "living with a parent or other adult related to him or her by blood,
-- marriage or adoption". Limbs 1 and 2 are the official's judgment, asked as facts; limb 3 is read as part of that judgment,
-- as the text places it there (NOTES.md finding 2).
GIVEN `age of the child` IS A NUMBER
      `the child is a full-time secondary or equivalent vocational student` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a child for family assistance` IF
        `age of the child` LESS THAN 18
    OR  (`age of the child` LESS THAN 19 AND `the child is a full-time secondary or equivalent vocational student`)

GIVEN `the applicant is pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a child for family assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child lives with the applicant, a parent or another adult relative by blood, marriage or adoption` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the official judges the allowance to be in the child's interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the official judges the applicant a fit person to bring up the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child was a New York resident on the date of application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `family assistance may be given under s 349` IF
        `the applicant is pregnant`
    OR  (    `there is a child for family assistance`
         AND `the child lives with the applicant, a parent or another adult relative by blood, marriage or adoption`
         AND `the official judges the allowance to be in the child's interest`
         AND `the official judges the applicant a fit person to bring up the child`
         AND `the child was a New York resident on the date of application`)

-- s 349 D: "Family assistance shall not be payable to a family for any month in which any caretaker relative with whom the
-- child is living is, on the last day of such month, participating in a strike".
GIVEN `a caretaker relative was on strike on the last day of the month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the strike rule bars the month` IF `a caretaker relative was on strike on the last day of the month`

§§ `s 131(6) -- a minor parent's living arrangement`

-- s 131(6): "No individual who is under the age of eighteen and is not married, who resides with and provides care for his
-- or her dependent child or is pregnant and otherwise entitled to family assistance shall receive family assistance for
-- himself or herself unless the individual ... resides in a place of residence maintained as a home by the individual's
-- parent, legal guardian or other adult relative or in an adult-supervised supportive living arrangement." The requirement
-- to live with a parent, guardian or adult relative does not apply under (a) to (e) (no such person living or known; none
-- allows it; serious harm or abuse there; imminent or serious harm; the child's best interests, as determined); but the
-- individual must then live in an approved adult-supervised supportive living arrangement "unless the individual's current
-- living arrangement is appropriate".
GIVEN `under 18 and unmarried` IS A BOOLEAN
      `caring for my own child, or pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I live in a home maintained by my parent, legal guardian or other adult relative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I live in an adult-supervised supportive living arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the exceptions in s 131(6)(a) to (e) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my current living arrangement is judged appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the minor parent rule allows family assistance for me` IF
        (NOT (`under 18 and unmarried` AND `caring for my own child, or pregnant`))
    OR  `I live in a home maintained by my parent, legal guardian or other adult relative`
    OR  `I live in an adult-supervised supportive living arrangement`
    OR  (`one of the exceptions in s 131(6)(a) to (e) applies` AND `my current living arrangement is judged appropriate`)

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant`
    `the social services district`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `hold a fair hearing`
    `give public assistance to the applicant`
    `pay the shelter allowance directly to the landlord`

-- s 131(6): "If a social services district denies assistance after a child alleges facts which, if true, would render this
-- subdivision inapplicable by reason of paragraph (c) or (d) ..., the applicant shall be entitled to a fair hearing pursuant
-- to section twenty-two of this chapter held within thirty days of the request, if the request is timely made." Days run
-- from the request.
GIVEN `the request is timely` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the minor parent's fair hearing` `the request is timely` MEANS
    IF `the request is timely`
    THEN PARTY `the social services district`
         MUST  `hold a fair hearing`
         WITHIN 30
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the social services district` BECAUSE "no fair hearing held within thirty days of the request (s 131(6))"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `s 131(10) -- voluntarily quitting a job to qualify`

-- s 131(10): "Any applicant who voluntarily terminated his or her employment or voluntarily reduced his or her earning
-- capacity for the purpose of qualifying for public assistance or a larger amount thereof shall be disqualified from
-- receiving such assistance for ninety days from such termination or reduction, unless otherwise required by federal law".
-- Days run from the termination; the district must not give assistance within them.
GIVEN `quit or reduced earnings to qualify` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the voluntary quit disqualification` `quit or reduced earnings to qualify` MEANS
    IF `quit or reduced earnings to qualify`
    THEN PARTY `the social services district`
         SHANT `give public assistance to the applicant`
         WITHIN 90
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the social services district` BECAUSE "assistance given within ninety days of a voluntary quit to qualify (s 131(10))"
    ELSE FULFILLED

GIVEN `the day I quit or reduced my earnings` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day the s 131(10) disqualification no longer applies` `the day I quit or reduced my earnings` MEANS
    `the day I quit or reduced my earnings` PLUS 90

§§ `s 350(2) -- the sixty-month limit`

-- s 350(2): assistance funded under the TANF block grant "(a) shall not be granted to any family which includes an adult who
-- has received any form of assistance funded in whole or in part under the temporary assistance to needy families block
-- grant program ... in this state or in any other state for a cumulative period of longer than sixty months", where (i)
-- months as "a minor child who was not the head of household or married to the head of household" are not counted, (ii) a
-- family is exempt "on the basis of hardship when the adult family member is unable to work because of an independently
-- verified physical or mental impairment including those resulting from domestic violence, or when the adult family member
-- is in receipt of supplemental security income payments ... or additional state payments", and (iii) months of cash
-- assistance in the safety net assistance program are counted.
GIVEN `months of TANF-funded or safety net cash assistance received as an adult` IS A NUMBER
      `the hardship exemption applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sixty-month limit bars TANF-funded family assistance` IF
        `months of TANF-funded or safety net cash assistance received as an adult` GREATER THAN 60
    AND (NOT `the hardship exemption applies`)

§§ `s 131-n(1) -- resources that are exempt`

-- s 131-n(1): exempt and disregarded: "(a) cash and liquid or nonliquid resources up to two thousand five hundred dollars for
-- applicants, three thousand seven hundred fifty dollars for applicants in households in which any member is sixty years of
-- age or older or is disabled or ten thousand dollars for recipients"; (b) up to $4,650 in a vehicle savings account and (c)
-- up to $1,400 in a tuition account, each opened while receiving assistance; (d) the home; (e) "one automobile, up to ...
-- twelve thousand dollars fair market value, beginning April first, two thousand eighteen ... or such other higher dollar
-- value as the local social services district may elect"; (f) burial plots; (g) funeral agreements up to $1,500 each;
-- (h) individual development accounts; (j) 529 plans; (k) ABLE accounts. Items (b)-(d), (f)-(k) are asked as one excluded
-- total: only the other resources and the car are asked.
GIVEN `already receiving public assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a household member is 60 or older or disabled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 131-n(1)(a) exempt amount` MEANS
    IF `already receiving public assistance`
    THEN 10000
    ELSE IF `a household member is 60 or older or disabled`
         THEN 3750
         ELSE 2500

GIVEN `already receiving public assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a household member is 60 or older or disabled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `cash and other resources not exempted by another paragraph` IS A NUMBER
      `fair market value of one automobile` IS A NUMBER
      `the district's automobile limit, if higher than $12,000` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`resources not exempted by s 131-n(1)` MEANS
    LET `car limit` MEANS IF `the district's automobile limit, if higher than $12,000` GREATER THAN 12000
                          THEN `the district's automobile limit, if higher than $12,000`
                          ELSE 12000
        `car excess` MEANS IF `fair market value of one automobile` GREATER THAN `car limit`
                           THEN `fair market value of one automobile` MINUS `car limit`
                           ELSE 0
        `total` MEANS `cash and other resources not exempted by another paragraph` PLUS `car excess`
        `exempt` MEANS `the s 131-n(1)(a) exempt amount` `already receiving public assistance` `a household member is 60 or older or disabled`
    IN IF `total` GREATER THAN `exempt` THEN `total` MINUS `exempt` ELSE 0

§§ `s 131-a(2), (3), (3-c), (3-d) -- the standard of need and the grant`

-- s 131-a(2)(a-4): "For the period beginning October first, two thousand twelve and thereafter, the following shall be the
-- standard of monthly need ...": One $158, Two $252, Three $336, Four $433, Five $534, Six $617; "For each additional person
-- in the household there shall be added an additional amount of eighty-five dollars monthly." s 131-a(3)(a-4) sets the same
-- figures as the "maximum monthly grants and allowances".
GIVEN `household size` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 131-a(2)(a-4) basic amount` `household size` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `household size` AT MOST 1 THEN 158
        IF `household size` EQUALS 2  THEN 252
        IF `household size` EQUALS 3  THEN 336
        IF `household size` EQUALS 4  THEN 433
        IF `household size` EQUALS 5  THEN 534
        OTHERWISE 617 PLUS (85 TIMES (`household size` MINUS 6))

-- s 131-a(3-c): "a home energy grant equal to the following monthly amounts": One $14.10, Two $22.50, Three $30.00, Four
-- $38.70, Five $47.70, Six $55.20, plus $7.50 for each additional needy person.
GIVEN `household size` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 131-a(3-c) home energy grant` `household size` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `household size` AT MOST 1 THEN 14.10
        IF `household size` EQUALS 2  THEN 22.50
        IF `household size` EQUALS 3  THEN 30.00
        IF `household size` EQUALS 4  THEN 38.70
        IF `household size` EQUALS 5  THEN 47.70
        OTHERWISE 55.20 PLUS (7.50 TIMES (`household size` MINUS 6))

-- s 131-a(3-d): "a monthly supplemental home energy grant": One $11, Two $17, Three $23, Four $30, Five $37, Six $42, plus
-- $5 for each additional needy person. (It is expressed as an increase to "the amounts set forth in paragraph (a) of
-- subdivision three", the pre-2009 schedule: NOTES.md finding 5.)
GIVEN `household size` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 131-a(3-d) supplemental home energy grant` `household size` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `household size` AT MOST 1 THEN 11
        IF `household size` EQUALS 2  THEN 17
        IF `household size` EQUALS 3  THEN 23
        IF `household size` EQUALS 4  THEN 30
        IF `household size` EQUALS 5  THEN 37
        OTHERWISE 42 PLUS (5 TIMES (`household size` MINUS 6))

-- s 131-a(2)(b): "In addition to the above, the standard of need shall include amounts for shelter and fuel for heating,
-- amounts for home energy payments (including amounts for supplemental home energy grants), ... and amounts for other items
-- when required by individual case circumstances". The shelter and fuel amounts are set by regulation (inputs).
-- (2)(e): "The standard of monthly need, when not a whole dollar amount, shall be rounded to the next lower whole dollar".
GIVEN `household size` IS A NUMBER
      `the shelter amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the fuel for heating amount` IS A NUMBER
      `other individual items` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the standard of monthly need` MEANS
    FLOOR (    `the s 131-a(2)(a-4) basic amount` `household size`
          PLUS `the s 131-a(3-c) home energy grant` `household size`
          PLUS `the s 131-a(3-d) supplemental home energy grant` `household size`
          PLUS `the shelter amount`
          PLUS `the fuel for heating amount`
          PLUS `other individual items`)

§§ `s 131-a(8) -- income that is disregarded`

-- s 131-a(8)(a): exempt and disregarded: "(i) all of the earned income of a dependent child ... who is a full-time student or
-- part-time student" (asked by leaving it out of the earnings); "(ii) fifty percent of the earned income for such month of
-- any recipient; provided, however, that such percentage amount shall be adjusted in June of each year" to the poverty
-- guidelines (the adjusted percentage is an input: NOTES.md finding 6); "(iii) ... one hundred fifty dollars of the earned
-- income for such month that remains after application of subparagraph (ii)"; "(v) the first one hundred dollars received in
-- such month which represent support payments timely paid in and for such month for one child, and the first two hundred
-- dollars ... for two or more children"; "(viii) any federal income taxes refunded by reason of section thirty-two" (the
-- federal EIC; asked by leaving it out); "(xiii) once during the lifetime of a recipient ..., all of the earned income ...
-- following job entry, ... for no more than six consecutive months" if total income is not more than 200% of the federal
-- poverty level (asked as one fact).
-- (b): no (ii) or (iii) disregard if the person "(i) terminated his employment or reduced his earned income without good
-- cause" within 75 days before the determination, "(ii) refused without good cause ... to accept employment", or "(iii)
-- failed without good cause to make a timely report ... of earned income received in the month a determination of need is
-- made". (c): no (iii) disregard "if the income of such person was in excess of his or her need, unless such person received
-- public assistance in one or more of the four months preceding the month of need determination".
GIVEN `monthly earned income` IS A NUMBER
      `the s 131-a(8)(a)(ii) percentage as adjusted in June` IS A NUMBER
      `a s 131-a(8)(b) bar applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the s 131-a(8)(c) bar applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lifetime job-entry disregard of s 131-a(8)(a)(xiii) applies this month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`countable earned income` MEANS
    IF `the lifetime job-entry disregard of s 131-a(8)(a)(xiii) applies this month`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `a s 131-a(8)(b) bar applies`
         THEN `monthly earned income`
         ELSE LET `after (ii)` MEANS `monthly earned income` MINUS (`the s 131-a(8)(a)(ii) percentage as adjusted in June` TIMES `monthly earned income`)
              IN  IF `the s 131-a(8)(c) bar applies`
                  THEN `after (ii)`
                  ELSE IF `after (ii)` GREATER THAN 150 THEN `after (ii)` MINUS 150 ELSE 0

GIVEN `support payments timely paid for this month` IS A NUMBER
      `the support is for two or more children` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`countable support payments` MEANS
    LET `disregard` MEANS IF `the support is for two or more children` THEN 200 ELSE 100
    IN  IF `support payments timely paid for this month` GREATER THAN `disregard`
        THEN `support payments timely paid for this month` MINUS `disregard`
        ELSE 0

-- s 131-a(8)(c) asks whether "the income of such person was in excess of his or her need" -- read as the gross income
-- before any disregard, against the standard of need (NOTES.md finding 7).
GIVEN `gross monthly income` IS A NUMBER
      `standard of need` IS A NUMBER
      `received public assistance in one of the four preceding months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 131-a(8)(c) bar is met` IF
        `gross monthly income` GREATER THAN `standard of need`
    AND (NOT `received public assistance in one of the four preceding months`)

§§ `s 131-a(1), (2)(d), (3)(b), (c) -- the monthly grant`

-- s 131-a(1): officials "shall ... provide public assistance to needy persons who ... are determined to be eligible in
-- accordance with standards of need established in subdivision two. Provision for such persons, for all items of need, less
-- any available income or resources which are not required to be disregarded ..., shall be made in accordance with this
-- section." (2)(d): a monthly need under ten dollars means the household is "not ... in need of cash assistance"; (3)(b):
-- "no payment of public assistance shall be made for any month if the amount of such payment would be less than ten
-- dollars"; (3)(c): the grant "when not a whole dollar amount, shall be rounded to the next lower whole dollar amount".
-- Countable resources are taken off the need for the month, as s 131-a(1) says (NOTES.md finding 8).
GIVEN `standard of need` IS A NUMBER
      `countable income` IS A NUMBER
      `countable resources` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the monthly grant` `standard of need` `countable income` `countable resources` MEANS
    LET `deficit` MEANS FLOOR (`standard of need` MINUS `countable income` MINUS `countable resources`)
    IN  IF `deficit` LESS THAN 10 THEN 0 ELSE `deficit`

-- s 131-a(1) as a duty of the district to the eligible household, monthly or semi-monthly; s 131-a(7): "Whenever a social
-- services official finds that a recipient of public assistance has failed to fully apply the amount allowed in his grant
-- for shelter to the payment of rent ..., unless rent is being withheld pursuant to law or court order, the social services
-- official shall furnish such recipient's shelter allowance in the form of direct payments to the owner".
GIVEN `the official finds the shelter allowance was not fully applied to rent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `rent is being withheld under law or court order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`direct payment of my shelter allowance` `the official finds the shelter allowance was not fully applied to rent` `rent is being withheld under law or court order` MEANS
    IF `the official finds the shelter allowance was not fully applied to rent` AND (NOT `rent is being withheld under law or court order`)
    THEN PARTY `the social services district`
         MUST  `pay the shelter allowance directly to the landlord`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED
